<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <div class="albert-card mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div class="rounded-lg border-2 border-red-600 bg-red-50 p-4 text-sm text-red-800">
      <strong>Draft — not legal advice.</strong>
      This document was drafted as a starting point and has not been reviewed by
      a lawyer. Data protection obligations (GDPR, CCPA, and others) depend on
      where your users and business are located. Have qualified counsel review
      and adapt this before relying on it for a real launch.
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 text-center text-sm text-black/60">Last updated: August 10, 2026</p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">1. What We Collect</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      When you create an account, search for flights, or make a booking, we
      collect: your email address; booking details (flight, seat, price); and
      messages you send us through the contact form. We do not collect or
      store your payment card details — those are handled directly by Stripe.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">2. How We Use It</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We use this information to: create and manage your account; process and
      confirm bookings; send booking confirmations and account-related emails
      (such as login links); and respond to messages you send us. We do not
      sell your personal information.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">3. Third Parties</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We share information with service providers only as needed to operate
      the service: Stripe (payment processing) and our email delivery
      provider (sending account and booking emails). Each processes data under
      their own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">4. Data Retention</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We retain account and booking information for as long as your account is
      active, or as needed to comply with legal, tax, or accounting
      obligations. [Specific retention periods must be defined based on
      applicable law.]
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">5. Your Rights</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
      or delete your personal information, or to object to certain processing.
      Contact us via the
      <.link href="/contact" class="text-[#2563eb] underline">Contact Us</.link>
      page to make a request.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">6. Cookies and Sessions</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We use a session cookie to keep you signed in. We do not use third-party
      advertising or tracking cookies at this time.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">7. Security</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Passwords are hashed and never stored in plain text. Payment processing
      is handled entirely by Stripe's PCI-compliant infrastructure — we never
      see or store full card numbers.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">8. Changes to This Policy</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes
      will be reflected by updating the date at the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">9. Contact</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Questions about this policy can be sent via our
      <.link href="/contact" class="text-[#2563eb] underline">Contact Us</.link>
      page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
